There is another element that breaks when using Ollama. 
Meilisearch is expecting the vector param to be under the key `embedding` when Ollama sends `embeddings`.

For now, I decided to switch to source `rest`, since `ollama` source does not accept the `request` and `response` params, and adjust those. Maybe we can also add this possibility for the source ollama.

For example, in a docker scenario, I have now:

```
curl -X PATCH "http://meilisearch:7700/indexes/example/settings" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --data-binary '{
        "embedders": {
            "default": {
                "source": "rest",
                "documentTemplate": "{{doc.text}}",
                "url": "http://ollama:11434/api/embed",
                "request": {
                    "model": "nomic-embed-text",
                    "input": "{{text}}"
                },
                "response": {
                    "embeddings": ["{{embedding}}"]
                }
            }
        }
    }'
```
